{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfeaNDmdwoGLT426hAMem","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The candidate passed the self-check: the check command printed `OK`. Novelty against the other models was not checked; that happens at admission.\n\n**Name:** `pair_normalized_alternation_contrast`\n\n**Hypothesis:** People judge the pair relative to itself. Each person still measures how far each sequence's switching rate is from their own ideal switching rate. But the gap between the two distances is divided by how far both sequences are from that ideal together, a Weber-like contrast normalisation. A given gap decides the choice sharply when both sequences are near the ideal and barely matters when both are far from it. So the same sequence is judged differently beside a different partner, which is the comparison effect the brief asked for.\n\n**Model:**\n- Each person's ideal switching rate is drawn from a population distribution, with 400 participant slots so the model can predict new people.\n- `beta` sets how strongly the contrast drives the choice.\n- `c` is a fitted constant added to the denominator; it sets how strongly the judgement depends on the pair. As `c` grows large, the model collapses back to the plain personal-ideal-distance model.\n- `p_left = sigmoid(beta · (d_b − d_a) / (c + d_a + d_b))`, where `d_a` and `d_b` are the squared distances of the left and right sequences from the person's ideal.\n\n**Check result:** The short fit (100 draws, one chain) gave an ELPD-LOO of −1105.4, close to the current models (best −1072, rank 2 −1084). Two warnings came with it:\n- **PSIS-LOO unreliable:** 3.1% of trials have Pareto k > 0.5, above the 1% tolerance, so the ELPD estimate may be inaccurate.\n- **Convergence not verified:** a single chain can't report R-hat. The full admission fit still has to pass the divergence, R-hat and ESS limits within 30 minutes.\n\nThe model doesn't include the incumbent's periodic-pattern penalty: I kept it to one mechanism. So it isn't expected to fix the critique's discrepancy about long streaks and regular patterns, only to test whether pair-relative contrast explains the choices better than judging each sequence on its own.\n\nFiles are in `/scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run2/data/subjective_randomness/experiment1/model_loop/iter_2/candidate_0`:\n- `hypothesis.md`\n- `model_name.txt`\n- `candidate.py`"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2463,"cache_read_input_tokens":54125,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2463,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"20d2da72-07b7-40aa-b4cf-68b0e912e167","uuid":"f55d4991-87d1-4781-944e-7f5a9d47b3d7","timestamp":"2026-10-03T03:15:05.815Z","request_id":"req_011CfeaNDNaK8bwXSbW8z3DG"}
